Q1 Largest of Three Numbers
Write a Python program that prompts the user to enter three integers. Print the largest of the three integers

# Prompt the user to enter three integers
a = int(input())
b = int(input())
c = int(input())

# Find and print the largest integer
largest = max(a, b, c)
print(largest)



Q2 Write a Python program to convert temperature from Celsius to Fahrenheit.

# Read temperature in Celsius
celsius = float(input())

# Convert to Fahrenheit
fahrenheit = (celsius * 9/5) + 32

# Print the result formatted to 2 decimal places
print(f"{fahrenheit:.2f}")


